.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH SSGRID 1 2000-1月 "perturb" "perturb"
.SH NAME
perturb \- run the in silico perturbation experiment on the fitted S-system network model
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIperturb(\fBnetwork\fR as <generic> SSystemNetwork, 
\fBgeneIds\fR as any, 
\fBtype\fR as string = "knockdown", 
\fBmagnitude\fR as double = 0.8, 
\fBkicks\fR as integer = 1, 
\fBstart\fR as double = 0.1, 
\fBfinal_time\fR as double = 0, 
\fBcontext\fR as list = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBexport\fR as string = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
run the in silico perturbation experiment on the fitted S-system network model
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBnetwork\fB \fR\- the fitted network model, which is the output of the \fBsfit\fR api.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgeneIds\fB \fR\- a character vector of the target gene id of the perturbation.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBtype\fB \fR\- 
 the perturbation type: \fBknockdown\fR(default), \fBknockout\fR or 
 \fBoverexpress\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmagnitude\fB \fR\- 
 the perturbation strength: for the knockdown, \fB0.8\fR means that the target 
 gene loses 80% of its activity; for the overexpress, \fB1\fR means that an 
 extra 100% of the baseline expression will be added to the target gene.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBkicks\fB \fR\- 
 the times that the perturbation will be applied, a periodic stimulation is 
 used to simulate a sustained treatment.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBstart\fB \fR\- the time point that the first perturbation kick is applied.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBfinal_time\fB \fR\- the final time of the simulation, zero means the end of the fitted time axis.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcontext\fB \fR\- 
 the optional sample context(the ODE initial state), which should be 
 created via the \fBsgrid_context\fR api.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBexport\fB \fR\- 
 the optional output directory for save the trajectory files of each 
 perturbation design; nothing will be written if this parameter is not 
 provided.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- -. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a [ScreeningResult](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.SGrid.Perturbation.ScreeningResult) object which could be converted to a 
 \fBdata.frame\fR via \fBas.data.frame\fR, or a R# error message object.
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
let ctx = sgrid_context(network, "/data/pseudobulk_context_A.csv");
 let resp = perturb(network, c("ABCD1","ACLY"), context = ctx, export = "/tmp/ko");
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
ssGrid
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
